WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.639
Episode 3. Last time, we moved

00:02.639 --> 00:04.680
from talented individuals to

00:04.680 --> 00:07.759
talented teams. Today, the second

00:07.759 --> 00:10.639
shift from transactions to moments

00:10.639 --> 00:11.520
that matter.

00:27.202 --> 00:29.442
This second shift makes moments

00:29.442 --> 00:31.121
that matter a core design

00:31.121 --> 00:32.922
principle of our future operating

00:32.922 --> 00:33.922
model.

00:33.922 --> 00:35.482
Moments where knowledge is shared

00:35.482 --> 00:37.202
across generations.

00:37.202 --> 00:38.881
Moments in a workplace designed

00:38.881 --> 00:40.682
for collective work.

00:40.682 --> 00:42.202
Simpler moments built for the

00:42.202 --> 00:44.202
human touch, not for process

00:44.202 --> 00:45.762
compliance.

00:45.762 --> 00:47.442
Moments that put the team at the

00:47.442 --> 00:49.602
center to drive engagement and

00:49.602 --> 00:50.562
performance.

00:50.603 --> 00:52.843
On the human and cultural side,

00:52.843 --> 00:54.242
people are looking for purpose at

00:54.242 --> 00:56.563
work. They expect recognition that

00:56.563 --> 00:59.483
feels real, not a yearly process.

00:59.483 --> 01:01.003
They need a new leadership that

01:01.003 --> 01:03.282
inspires a growth mindset

01:03.282 --> 01:04.843
and workplace moments must bring

01:04.843 --> 01:06.242
back a sense of collective

01:06.242 --> 01:08.403
belonging in real life.

01:08.564 --> 01:10.484
On paper, these moments already

01:10.484 --> 01:13.284
exist, people reviews, a flexible

01:13.284 --> 01:15.604
workplace, and leaders who engage

01:15.604 --> 01:16.604
their teams.

01:16.765 --> 01:19.284
But too often reality falls short.

01:19.284 --> 01:21.325
People reviews turn into scattered

01:21.325 --> 01:24.285
box ticking HR tasks. Office days

01:24.285 --> 01:26.485
are about presence not purpose.

01:26.485 --> 01:28.565
And legacy leadership models fail

01:28.565 --> 01:30.565
to unlock collective intelligence

01:30.565 --> 01:32.965
and end up draining engagement.

01:32.966 --> 01:35.406
So we flip the dynamic, simplify

01:35.406 --> 01:37.446
the transaction, elevate the

01:37.446 --> 01:38.646
moment.

01:38.646 --> 01:41.046
In people reviews, AI takes notes

01:41.046 --> 01:42.966
and summarizes and suggests the

01:42.966 --> 01:44.525
development paths and missions

01:44.525 --> 01:46.966
worth discussing. In the workplace,

01:46.966 --> 01:48.525
onsite time is for knowledge

01:48.525 --> 01:51.206
transfer across generations captured

01:51.206 --> 01:53.726
by an AI agent and for debriffs

01:53.726 --> 01:55.526
that drive improvement.

01:55.526 --> 01:57.565
And leaders dare to unlearn and

01:57.565 --> 01:59.886
reinvent, focusing on team bonding

01:59.886 --> 02:03.005
spirit like elite sport coaches.

02:03.005 --> 02:04.325
moments that put people back at

02:04.325 --> 02:06.886
the center powered by AI because

02:06.886 --> 02:08.045
in the end, the real

02:08.045 --> 02:09.525
differentiator will be human

02:09.525 --> 02:11.446
performance. People working as a

02:11.446 --> 02:15.126
team, engaged, learning continuously

02:15.126 --> 02:16.926
and adapting fast.

02:17.207 --> 02:20.287
But AI is not magic. It takes a

02:20.287 --> 02:21.686
method.

02:21.686 --> 02:24.246
That is the next shift from tech

02:24.246 --> 02:27.646
magic to lean AI transformation.

02:27.646 --> 02:29.007
See you in episode 4.
